gcOffMainT -- SEQ 589 (GC stroke 2, R2, Tony, 2026-11-10): the engine base refuses an allocation off the main thread.

offMainProbe (gcThreads.mm, gcOffMainProbe) constructs a GroupItem on a pthread of its own, named offMainProbe. gcEngine's
new sees it is not the main thread, prints one line naming itself, the size and the thread, and aborts. So this run
ENDS at the probe: exit 134 (SIGABRT), OM-1 printed, the refusal line on stderr, and neither OM-2 nor the sentinel --
the sentinel here is the H7: if the refusal is removed, OM-2 and the sentinel print and the exit is 0.

Why a probe and not a real case: nothing in the engine allocates off the main thread today (docs/gcRecon.md 3c --
GroupItem::dispatch() is parked with no callers), so no fixture could reach the refusal any other way.
